/addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUGIYAMA, NAOKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATO HOZUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEKIGUCHI MANABU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUGIYAMA NAOKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, HOZUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEKIGUCHI, MANABU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUGIYAMA, NAOKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Oxetane compounds represented by general formula (1), which are excellent in radical polymerizability and cationic polymerizability and in compatibility and copolymerizability with other copolymerizable monomers; a process for producing the compounds; and an oxetane copolymer which is excellent in compatibility among the monomer units and has a low water absorption and excellent transparency. [In general formula (1), substituent R&lt;1&gt; is hydrogen, alkyl, fluorine, fluoroalkyl, allyl, aryl, furyl, or thienyl; substituents R&lt;2&gt;, R&lt;3&gt;, and R&lt;4&gt; each independently is hydrogen or C1-6 alkyl; and m and n each is an integer of 1 to 10 (provided that not all of R&lt;2&gt;, R&lt;3&gt;, and R&lt;4&gt; are hydrogen)].</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des composés d'oxétane de formule générale (1) qui se prêtent parfaitement à la polymérisation radicalaire, à la polymérisation cationique et sont compatibles et copolymérisables avec d'autres monomères copolymérisables. L'invention concerne aussi un procédé d'obtention des composés et un copolymère d'oxétane présentant une compatibilité excellente parmi les unités monomères, une absorption d'eau faible et une transparence excellente. Dans la formule générale (1), le substituant R&lt;1&gt; représente un hydrogène, alkyle, fluor, fluoroalkyle, allyle, aryle, furyle ou thiényle; les substituants R&lt;2&gt;, R&lt;3&gt; et R&lt;4&gt; représentent chacun un hydrogène ou un alkyle C1-6; et m et n représentent chacun un entier compris entre 1 et 190 (à condition qu'au moins un des R&lt;2&gt;, R&lt;3&gt; et R&lt;4&gt; ne soit pas un hydrogène).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>